    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The edge $\overline{e}$ defines a map $\Delta ^1 \rightarrow \calD $. Note that the fiber of the Kan fibration $\Hom ^{\rght }_{\calC }(X,Y) \rightarrow \Hom ^{\rght }_{\calD }(pX, pY)$ does not change if we replace $p$ by the induced projection $\calC \times _{\calD } \Delta ^1 \rightarrow \Delta ^1$. We may therefore assume without loss of generality that $e$ is $p$-Cartesian, and the desired result follows from the above analysis. 
